# Test via Makefile

When running this repo’s tests, use the Makefile — do not invent ad-hoc
`cargo test` / `pytest` command lines for the full suites.

| Goal | Recipe |
|------|--------|
| Both languages (default) | `make test` |
| Rust only | `make test-rust` |
| Rust + `python` feature | `make test-rust-python` |
| Python forest suite (no legacy) | `make test-python` |
| Legacy archive + native↔legacy | `make test-python-legacy` |
| CI non-test gates | `make check` |

These mirror `.github/workflows/test.yml`. Narrow filters (`cargo test --lib foo`,
`pytest path::test`) are fine for debugging a single failure; put the full
suite back through `make` when checking green.

**Before pushing / cutting a tag:** run `make check` (fmt, clippy ×2, WASM
build, ruff, pyright) — `make test*` does not cover those gates.

**Legacy:** `tests/forest/legacy` and native↔legacy `test_parity.py` are
**not** on CI or default `make test` / `make test-python`. Use
`make test-python-legacy` when you need them.
